# Documentation Rules

- Write new documentation in English.
- Keep operational instructions concise and immediately actionable.
- Update docs when behavior, setup, or runbook steps change.
- Prefer short sections and bullet lists over long prose.

# Agent Instruction Consistency

- Keep `AGENTS.md` aligned with project behavior and tooling.
- When adding workflow steps, include clear safety boundaries and verification checkpoints.
- Avoid duplicating large manuals; link or reference canonical files instead.
